// The third file of the hello world, and the only one that can run.
//
// `saluta` returns the greeting and can do nothing else; `imprime_gutenbergio`
// writes whatever its writer can write. Neither has any authority of its own.
// This is where authority enters: once, as the `Mundus` parameter §4.1 rule 2
// names, and everything below it is derived from that value. There is no
// `poscit` clause because there is nothing to draw from an enclosing scope --
// a program's root has no enclosing scope (§4.7).
//
// The standard streams are `ambitus`, the process environment, not `archivum`
// (§4.6): writing to a terminal touches nothing on a filesystem, and the audit
// in §10.3 should say so.
//
// `[UNTESTED]` -- this parses and builds a typed AST; nothing checks or runs it
// yet (spec §16, Stages 2 and 3). `Scriptor` is the standard writer type that
// the runtime prelude supplies; its shape is pinned in docs/design/runtime.md.

publica functio initium(m: Mundus) -> u8 {
    firma a = m.ambitus();
    sub ambitus = a;
    firma s = Scriptor.ad_exitum(a);
    imprime_gutenbergio(s, saluta());
    redde 0;
}
